# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# AI Tutor — Frontend environment variables (Vite)
#
# Copy this file to `frontend/.env` for LOCAL development, and add the SAME
# variable names in the VERCEL dashboard (Project → Settings → Environment
# Variables) for production. Only VITE_* variables reach the browser.
#
# Private values (keys, IDs) are left blank — fill them in at deploy time.
# The app name / URLs are taken care of by the repo:
#   * Backend URL: NONE needed — `frontend/vercel.json` rewrites `/api/*`
#     to your Render backend, and `frontend/src/lib/api.js` calls `/api`.
#   * App title/branding: `frontend/index.html` (+ `public/manifest.json`)
#     already use "AI Tutor"; change them there if you rename the app.
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ── Email (verification / password-reset / invites / digest) ──────────────
# Sent from the BROWSER via smtp.js (smtpjs.com) — no EmailJS needed.
# WARNING: these values end up in the browser bundle (VITE_* = public), so
# use a dedicated sending account (Gmail + App Password) — never your
# personal password.
VITE_SMTP_HOST=smtp.gmail.com              # e.g. smtp.gmail.com
VITE_SMTP_USER=                            # your sending account, e.g. youraddress@gmail.com
VITE_SMTP_PASSWORD=                        # Gmail App Password (Google > Security > 2-Step Verification > App passwords)
VITE_SMTP_FROM=AI Tutor <youraddress@gmail.com>

# ── Google "Continue with Google" (optional) ──────────────────────────────
# Must be the SAME Google OAuth Client ID as GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID on Render
# (Google Cloud Console → Credentials → OAuth 2.0 Client). Leave blank to
# hide the Google button entirely.
# https://console.cloud.google.com/apis/credentials
VITE_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=

# ── Local development only (optional) ─────────────────────────────────────
# When running `npm run dev` against the remote backend, the /api rewrite in
# vercel.json does not apply — Vite proxies here. Create ONE of these blocks:
#   VITE_DEV_API_URL=https://ai-digital-tutor.onrender.com
#   (production builds always use /api + vercel.json rewrite — do not set
#    VITE_DEV_API_URL in Vercel)